        {"q": "Which OSI layer handles MAC addressing and switching?", "options": ["Layer 1 — transmits raw bits over the physical medium using cables and signals", "Layer 2 — handles MAC addresses and forwards frames between devices on the same network", "Layer 3 — routes packets based on IP addresses between different networks", "Layer 4 — provides reliable end-to-end data delivery using TCP or UDP"], "answer": "Layer 2 — handles MAC addresses and forwards frames between devices on the same network"},
        {"q": "Which protocol operates at the Transport layer and provides reliable delivery?", "options": ["UDP — connectionless protocol that sends data without guaranteeing delivery or order", "IP — routes packets across networks based on destination IP address", "TCP — provides reliable, ordered delivery using acknowledgements and retransmission", "ICMP — used for network diagnostics and error reporting between devices"], "answer": "TCP — provides reliable, ordered delivery using acknowledgements and retransmission"},
