        {"q": "What does a router use to make forwarding decisions?", "options": ["MAC address table — used by switches to forward frames on the local network segment", "ARP cache — maps IP addresses to MAC addresses for local network communication", "Routing table — contains network prefixes and next-hop addresses for packet forwarding", "DNS records — maps hostnames to IP addresses for name resolution services"], "answer": "Routing table — contains network prefixes and next-hop addresses for packet forwarding"},
        {"q": "What is the key difference between static and dynamic routing?", "options": ["Static routing is always faster because it uses dedicated hardware acceleration circuits", "Dynamic routes are manually configured by an administrator and never change automatically", "Static routes are manually configured; dynamic routes are learned and updated automatically", "Static and dynamic routing use identical mechanisms but different administrative interfaces"], "answer": "Static routes are manually configured; dynamic routes are learned and updated automatically"},
